    // @item fn:outram_park_fork_dwsim_libs::clean_energies::solar_panel::generated_power
#[doc = "Electrical power generated by a photovoltaic array —\n`SolarPanel.vb:264`.\n\n`P = G * A * N * eta`\n\n# Inputs\n\n- `irradiance` — plane-of-array irradiance `G` \\[W/m²\\]. Physically\n  `0` to about `1400` W/m² at the Earth's surface; the standard-test\n  reference is 1000 W/m². DWSIM stores it in kW/m² with a default of 1.0\n  (`:56`), i.e. 1000 W/m².\n- `panel_area` — the area `A` of **one** panel \\[m²\\]. DWSIM default 1 m²\n  (`:48`).\n- `number_of_panels` — how many identical panels `N` (`:52`, default 1).\n- `efficiency` — DC conversion efficiency `eta`, dimensionless in `[0, 1]`.\n  DWSIM stores this as a **percentage** with default 15 (`:50`) and\n  divides by 100 at `:264`; this port takes the fraction directly, so pass\n  `0.15` where DWSIM's editor shows `15`. Typical values: 0.06-0.13\n  (thin film), 0.15-0.22 (crystalline silicon).\n\nThe relation is exactly linear in every argument — doubling irradiance,\narea or panel count doubles the output. Returns watts."]
#[pyfunction(name = "generated_power")]
